It will depend on how long the cat was in the box. The admixture of a dead
cat grows with time. Nethack could implement it by adding an additional flag
to a QM box ('cat is alive') and then getting a random number each turn and 
flipping the flag with some low probability. At the moment the flag flips
a cat corpse should be created in the box. If you open the box when the flag
is still 'alive' the game should create a tame cat next to you (and the box 
would be trapped in that case ;-). 

Now this is probably silly and not worth implementing...
